Clean. Let's do a final review of the diff and git status to confirm the working tree reflects exactly the intended remediation.
Remediation complete for what's achievable within `crates/`; one piece of finding 2 is structurally blocked outside my scope. Summary:

**Finding 1 (scope-outside-crates) — resolved.**
- `tests/fixtures/repo-rust-cli/` and `repo-node-service/` → `crates/fixtures/...`
- `docs/acceptance/PRD-038-multi-repo-have-at-it.md` → `crates/docs/acceptance/PRD-038-multi-repo-have-at-it.md`
- Updated both `multi_repo_acceptance.rs` test files' `copy_fixture_repository` to resolve `CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR/../fixtures/<name>` instead of the old workspace-root `../../tests/fixtures`, and fixed the one path reference inside the doc.
- Verified: `cargo test -p familiar-ai-daemon --test multi_repo_acceptance` → 13/13 pass; `-p familiar-ai-mcp` → 4/4 pass; `cargo fmt --all -- --check` clean; `cargo clippy -p familiar-ai-daemon -p familiar-ai-mcp --all-targets` clean. All changes now sit entirely under `crates/`.

**Finding 2 (acceptance-tests-uncovered) — partially addressed, one part structurally out of scope.**
- I got fresh, real evidence the new acceptance tests pass (above) — that resolves the "unverifiable" concern for the tests themselves.
- The remediation asks for two things: (a) add the new crates to the required `tests-green-crates` check, and (b) fix why `tests-workspace-advisory` is red. Neither is fixable from inside `crates/`:
  - (a) The check command isn't defined anywhere in this repo (it's owned by the orchestrator's verification-plan config), so there's no in-scope file to edit.
  - (b) I traced the `tests-workspace-advisory` failure to two **pre-existing** tests in `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/run.rs` (`prd_over_budget_fails_before_history_and_agent`, `prompt_places_stable_context_before_volatile_prd`) — untouched by this diff, and they pass in a real git checkout (confirmed locally) but fail in Docker because root `.dockerignore` excludes `.git/`, so `/app` has no git repo and `git rev-parse` fails. The fix lives in `.dockerignore`/`Dockerfile` at the repo root — outside `allowed_paths: ["crates/"]`. Editing it would violate the scope constraint, so I left it alone rather than force a fix.

Nothing has been committed — the working tree just has the relocation/path-fix changes described above, staged renames plus unstaged edits. Flagging the Docker `.git` exclusion issue back for a human/orchestrator decision since it needs a path outside `crates/`.
